      "quote_id": "qt_9d834c6eacbb",
      "section_id": "sec_429cbe085a48",
      "text": "In contrast to Amdahl's law, which assumes a fixed problem size and yields pessimistic scaling, Gustafson's law assumes that problem sizes grow with available computing resources, allowing far greater effective speedup from parallel execution."
    },
